Create or verify a release evidence bundle

Usage: mantle release [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  create                           Create a release evidence bundle from local artifacts
  verify                           Verify a release evidence bundle using bundle-local contents only
  transport                        Pack, inspect, or unpack an opt-in chaptered release transport
  function-address-bind            Bind bundle-local function-address evidence into a Cairn-ready Mantle receipt
  reproduce                        Rebuild and compare published release artifacts, then write a reproducibility report
  global-reproducibility           Evaluate a digest-bound universe before making any global reproducibility claim
  global-reproducibility-evidence  Derive global reproducibility surface evidence from a verified release bundle
  gauntlet                         Validate, canonicalize, and aggregate reproducibility gauntlet evidence
  nix-witness                      Compare release bundle artifacts against located Nix-built artifacts and emit a Nix witness receipt
  attest                           Create and sign a release attestation for a verified release bundle
  witness-export                   Export a portable witness-request directory from verified public artifacts
  witness-rebuild                  Replay an exported witness request into witness sidecars and rebuild audit evidence
  help                             Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -v, --verbose                      Enable verbose logging
      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>        Log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
      --json                         Emit errors as JSON objects for tooling integration
      --store <STORE>                Where to export final build outputs on disk. Intermediate deps stay in castore. Source inputs always come from /nix/store. If not writable, builds still succeed (outputs in castore) [default: /nix/store]
      --store-prefix <STORE_PREFIX>  Logical store path prefix for derivation hashes. All output paths and ATerm hashes are computed against this prefix. Default: /mantle/store. Use --nix-compat for /nix/store [default: /mantle/store]
      --nix-compat                   Shorthand for --store-prefix=/nix/store. For interop testing with Nix-computed derivations
      --state-dir <STATE_DIR>        State directory for pathinfo.redb, blobs, and logs. Default: legacy $CRUNCH_STATE_DIR or $XDG_STATE_HOME/crunch or ~/.local/state/crunch. Use --state-dir for an explicit Mantle path
      --base-store <BASE_STORES>     Ordered list of read-only base store state directories for overlay composition. Declared in priority order (base A before base B)
  -h, --help                         Print help
